    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d180">

                <pb facs="0599" n="477" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg477"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr.
                            Edwardes.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-07-22"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 22,
                        1889</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Sir Julian Pauncefote’s note
                    of the 22d of May last, concerning the case of certain British subjects who were
                    not allowed to land from the steam-ship <hi rendition="#italic">Obdam</hi> at
                    the port of New York on the ground that they were contract laborers, I now have
                    the honor to inclose for your information a copy of a letter from the Secretary
                    of the Treasury sustaining the action of the collector in refusing to allow the
                    persons in question to laud.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F.
                    Wharton.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d180-a1.xml" xpointer="d180-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
